          "settings": {
            "question": "Practicing Esthetician:",
            "answer": "<p>For the practicing Esthetician conducting multi-step facials, maintaining posture while accessing the neck and upper décolleté is essential to preventing chronic shoulder fatigue. The integrated 15° tilt function rotates the seat back to open the working angle, bringing the client’s head closer to the operator without requiring forward stooping. This structural adjustment stabilizes practitioner mechanics, keeping hands precise during delicate extraction or peel applications.</p>"
          }
        },
        "application_2": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Lash Technicians and Microblading Specialists:",
            "answer": "<p>For certified Lash Technicians and Microblading Specialists, client head stability during extended 2-to-3-hour appointments directly impacts line precision and service efficiency. The Aero-Comfort features an adjustable, contoured headrest combined with manual reclining control, allowing the practitioner to establish fixed focal lengths and eliminate neck strain. The stable surface prevents micro-movements, ensuring a controlled environment for intricate facial work.</p>"
          }
        },
        "application_3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Clinical Spa Therapists:",
            "answer": "<p>For Clinical Spa Therapists carrying out post-procedure recovery protocols or body waxing, quick turnaround and equipment adaptability are crucial for clinic workflow. The high-durability, ultra-resistant leatherette surface cleans rapidly between sessions without deteriorating, while the manual height adjustment range (28.5\" to 33.5\") allows different technicians to share the same station seamlessly throughout high-volume clinic days.</p>"
          }
        }
